# Repositories whose pull requests this project reviews.
# SECURITY_REVIEWER_REPOS overrides FACTORY_REPOS when set, even to empty.
# Both unset, or the override set but empty: the channel still boots with no
# repositories, and a pull request delivery fails with an error naming both
# variables.
# SECURITY_REVIEWER_REPOS=owner/other
FACTORY_REPOS=cursor-demo-lab/marsbank
# Jira project keys. A draft PR is reviewed only when its head branch or
# title starts with one of these keys followed by a number (TLSSN-8-...,
# "TLSSN-8: ..."), which is how the factory names its PRs. Unset: every
# draft waits for ready_for_review.
FACTORY_JIRA_PROJECTS=TLSSN
# Host model. Unset: Auto (auto-smart, optimize_for=balanced), which takes
# no effort or speed. FACTORY_AGENT_MODEL=grok-4.7 defaults to effort high and
# speed fast. Effort and speed are params, never an id suffix.
FACTORY_AGENT_MODEL=
FACTORY_AGENT_EFFORT=
FACTORY_AGENT_SPEED=
# Stage. Unset, production, or prod: a live slug. Any other value (staging)
# is a staging slug that refuses the production Slack intake, Jira project,
# and sandbox repository (agent/lib/factory-stage.ts) unless
# FACTORY_STAGING_ALLOW_PRODUCTION names them, comma-separated.
FACTORY_ENV=
FACTORY_STAGING_ALLOW_PRODUCTION=
# Ops failure funnel (agent/lib/ops-funnel.ts), optional. A kv failure the
# code swallows logs one {"kv":"warn"} line either way. With both set, an
# unexpected kv or claim failure also posts one line per site and reason per
# hour to FACTORY_OPS_SLACK_CHANNEL (a C... id) as the separate chat:write-only
# ops bot, never the desk's token. Either unset: no post. FACTORY_OPS_FUNNEL=off
# turns the posts off.
FACTORY_OPS_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
FACTORY_OPS_SLACK_CHANNEL=
FACTORY_OPS_FUNNEL=
